WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
A pair of old scales.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.920
On one pan, a wedding ring drops.

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.980
On the other, a small purse and a key.

4
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.930
The scales tip one way, then the other.

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.790
In the 1840s, a wife's property and
earnings belonged to her husband.

6
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.540
And Jane, a governess,
earns 30 pounds a year.

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.130
So when her story ends, is
Jane free, or just married?

8
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.670
In this mission, you'll find out what the
law let a Victorian wife own, and why.

9
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.790
You'll follow Jane's money and work, from
a governess's wage to a village school.

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.540
And you'll judge each choice she makes.

11
00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.410
Dependent on others, or independent?

12
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.280
Your mission: decide whether
Jane ends the novel free.
